{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794358601589,"sessionID":"ses_e380d61b4ffect0alGKeoUVSaW","part":{"id":"prt_1c81b6746001e7IswOyzLdm8pl","messageID":"msg_1c81a9d5a001bHBrfG8TtBHIhA","sessionID":"ses_e380d61b4ffect0alGKeoUVSaW","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794358601590,"sessionID":"ses_e380d61b4ffect0alGKeoUVSaW","part":{"id":"prt_1c81b6750001MvKTwjq4txx5f7","messageID":"msg_1c81a9d5a001bHBrfG8TtBHIhA","sessionID":"ses_e380d61b4ffect0alGKeoUVSaW","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Build an incident center: Flask JSON API under `/api` (auth, incidents, timeline, public stats, SLA logic, SQLite in `./data`) plus a React/TypeScript/Vite frontend styled with Tailwind CSS, served by the same backend on port 8000 per the full spec in the conversation.\n\n## Important Details\n- Stack: Python 3.13 Flask (deps `flask==3.1.3`, `gunicorn==26.2.0` in `backend/requirements.txt`, hash-locked in `backend/requirements.lock`); React 19 + Vite 8 frontend in `frontend/`; `npm run build` must stay `vite build` writing `frontend/dist`.\n- Tailwind v4 installed exactly: `tailwindcss@4.3.5`, `@tailwindcss/vite@4.3.5` (devDeps, `--save-exact`); also `typescript@5.9.3`, `@types/react@19.3.0`, `@types/react-dom@19.3.0`. TS is NOT in the build script; verify types manually with `npx tsc --noEmit`.\n- Only CSS file allowed: `frontend/src/index.css` containing `@import \"tailwindcss\";`.\n- SLA: sev1=60, sev2=240, sev3=1440, sev4=4320 minutes; `sla_due_at` = opened_at + target of current severity; `sla_breached` = resolved_at > due OR (unresolved AND now > due), strict `>`.\n- Open/unresolved defined as `resolved_at IS NULL` (used by `open` filter and public stats).\n- Statuses enum: `investigating, identified, mitigating, monitoring, resolved`; severities: `sev1..sev4`.\n- PATCH accepts: title, service, commander, impact_summary, severity, status, opened_at, resolved_at (nullable, status syncs to it, reopen via status leaving `resolved`); ignores id/opened_by/reopen_count/sla fields/unknown keys; status change appends `status_change` event message `Status changed from {old} to {new}`; new status `resolved` sets `resolved_at`; leaving resolved clears it and increments `reopen_count`.\n- Response shapes are strict: incident = 13 exact keys; event = `{id,type,message,created_at,author}`; list = `{items,total,page,page_size}`; timeline = `{items}`; stats = `{open_total,open_by_severity,sla_breached_open,resolved_last_30_days}`; login = exactly `{token}`; errors = `{error,message,errors?}`.\n- Status codes: register 201, duplicate username 409, login 401 (any failure), invalid validation 400, create incident/timeline POST 201, PATCH 200, missing 401/404, unknown `/api` path 404 JSON, wrong method 405 JSON.\n- Incident create requires `title` (non-empty str) and `severity` (enum); service/commander/impact_summary optional default `\"\"`; optional `opened_at`; status forced to `investigating`.\n- Timeline POST: `message` required non-empty; `type` optional default `\"note\"`; free-form; author = signed-in user.\n- List defaults: page=1, page_size=50 (no cap); filters `severity`, `status`, `open` (true/false/1/0/yes/no), `q` (literal substring over title/service/commander/impact_summary with LIKE escaping), invalid enum/param → 400; order `opened_at DESC, id DESC`.\n- Auth: Bearer token in `Authorization`, tokens in SQLite `tokens` table (werkzeug password hashing); 401 without valid token on all incident/timeline endpoints; public: health, register, login, `/api/public/stats`.\n- Frontend has NO react-router — custom router (`navigate`, `usePath`, `Link` via history.pushState/popstate); token+username in localStorage (`incident_center_token`, `incident_center_username`); after register, frontend auto-calls login.\n- Routes: `/` public stats, `/login`, `/register`, `/incidents` (list, page_size=10), `/incidents/new`, `/incidents/{id}`.\n- Sandbox rules: only `/tmp/opencode/*` accessible (writes there were denied anyway); no docker available; pip/npm work via local registry proxy. Use `.server.log`, `.smoke.py` in workspace (clean up later).\n- Pitfall learned: never combine kill+restart of the dev server in one shell command containing the server's cmdline string (self-kills); use `pkill -f \"python3 back\"\"end/app.py\"` style or split calls.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Backend `backend/app.py` fully written: SQLite (`data/incident_center.db`, WAL), schema (users/tokens/incidents/timeline_events), auth, all endpoints, SLA computation, SPA catch-all serving `frontend/dist`, JSON 404/405 handlers, `init_db()` at import, dev runner on port 8000.\n- Backend verified: `/workspace/.smoke.py` (urllib test harness) prints `ALL API TESTS PASSED` covering register/login/401/create/validation/filters/pagination/patch/SLA/reopen/timeline/stats edge cases; extra curl checks confirm unknown `/api` → 404 JSON, `/api/incidents/abc` → 404, wrong method → 405 JSON, explicit `resolved_at` patch syncs status to `resolved` + appends status_change event.\n- Frontend tooling set up: deps installed (package.json/package-lock updated), `frontend/vite.config.ts` with `tailwindcss()` plugin, `frontend/tsconfig.json` (strict, noEmit, noUnusedLocals, verbatimModuleSyntax), `frontend/index.html` titled \"Incident Center\", `frontend/src/index.css`, `frontend/src/main.tsx` (imports `./index.css`).\n- Frontend source written: `src/api.ts` (types, ApiError, session, fetch wrapper), `src/auth.tsx` (AuthProvider/useAuth), `src/router.tsx` (navigate/usePath/Link), `src/ui.tsx` (SeverityBadge, StatusBadge, BreachBadge, ErrorAlert, Field, PageHeader, formatDate, inputClass, button classes, SEVERITIES/STATUSES consts), `src/App.tsx` (RequireAuth, Navbar with username + Sign out + \"Open incident\" button, route switch), `src/pages/PublicPage.tsx` (stats cards), `src/pages/AuthPage.tsx` (login/register forms with API error display), `src/pages/IncidentListPage.tsx` (severity/status filters, open-only switch, search, paging, breached rows).\n- Dev server currently running in background from earlier (`python3 backend/app.py > .server.log`), with test data in `data/`.\n\n### Active\n- Writing remaining frontend pages: `src/pages/NewIncidentPage.tsx` and `src/pages/IncidentDetailPage.tsx` (both imported by `src/App.tsx` but not yet created — build will fail until done).\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Write `frontend/src/pages/NewIncidentPage.tsx` (form: title/service/severity/commander/impact_summary, shows API `error` + per-field `errors`, navigates to `/incidents/{id}` on success) and `frontend/src/pages/IncidentDetailPage.tsx` (fields grid, status buttons PATCHing status, timeline list, post-event form, breach badge).\n2. Run `npx tsc --noEmit` in `frontend/`, fix type errors, then `npm run build`, restart backend, and verify end-to-end (curl HTML shell + assets); clean up `.smoke.py`, `.server.log`, and `data/` test data afterwards.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/workspace/backend/app.py`: complete Flask API + frontend host (done, tested).\n- `/workspace/backend/requirements.txt`, `/workspace/backend/requirements.lock`: pinned deps; do not add new backend deps.\n- `/workspace/Dockerfile`, `/workspace/README.md`, `/workspace/.dockerignore`: build contract (port 8000, `./data`, npm ci, requirements.lock constraints).\n- `/workspace/frontend/package.json`, `/workspace/frontend/package-lock.json`: deps incl. Tailwind 4.3.5, TS 5.9.3.\n- `/workspace/frontend/vite.config.ts`: react + tailwindcss plugins, `/api` proxy to `localhost:8000`.\n- `/workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json`, `/workspace/frontend/src/index.css`: TS config + Tailwind entry.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx`: router/Navbar — imports pages that must all exist.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/pages/`: PublicPage, AuthPage, IncidentListPage done; NewIncidentPage + IncidentDetailPage pending.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/api.ts`, `auth.tsx`, `router.tsx`, `ui.tsx`: shared client library.\n- `/workspace/.smoke.py`: API test harness (keep until final verification, then delete).\n- `/workspace/.server.log`: dev server log (delete at end).","time":{"start":1794358601552,"end":1794358601556}}}
